CROSS-EXAMINATION TRANSCRIPT - KEY EXCERPTS

PW-1 (Wife of Deceased):

Q: You stated that your husband told you about the assault before dying.
A: Yes.

Q: Was this statement recorded by any Magistrate?
A: No, it was not.

Q: Was any doctor called to certify that your husband was in a fit state of mind to make a statement?
A: No doctor was called.

Q: You did not inform any neighbour or police about this statement immediately?
A: I informed the police when they came next morning.

Q: So there is a gap of several hours between the alleged statement and its reporting?
A: Yes, but I was in shock.

PW-2 (Last-seen Witness):

Q: You stated that you saw the deceased with the accused at 22:45 hours.
A: Yes, that is correct.

Q: But in your 161 statement recorded on 15.03.2025, you mentioned the time as 21:30 hours.
A: I may have made a mistake.

Q: Which time is correct - 21:30 or 22:45?
A: I think it was around 22:45.

Q: Were the accused carrying any weapon when you saw them?
A: I did not see any weapon.

Q: Did you hear any sounds of altercation?
A: No, I did not hear anything.

Q: Then how do you know there was an altercation?
A: I assumed there was because of the land dispute.

INVESTIGATING OFFICER:

Q: You recovered the wooden stick on 16.03.2025 at 14:20 hours.
A: Yes.

Q: When was it sent to FSL?
A: On 18.03.2025.

Q: Why was there a delay of 48 hours?
A: We were busy with other investigation work.

Q: Was the weapon kept in proper custody during this period?
A: Yes, it was in the malkhana.

Q: Who had access to the malkhana during these 48 hours?
A: Several police officials have access.

Q: Was any entry made in the malkhana register regarding this weapon?
A: I am not sure about the entry.

Q: Were any independent witnesses present during the recovery?
A: No, only police officials were present.